                            <h2 class="key-highlights-title">Key Takeaways</h2>
                            <div class="key-highlights-content">
                                <ul>
	<li dir="ltr">
	<p dir="ltr" style="text-align:justify">Candlestick patterns are visual representations of the fluctuations of assetsâ€™ prices in trading.</p>
	</li>
	<li dir="ltr">
	<p dir="ltr" style="text-align:justify">The candlestick patterns cheat sheet presents single, double, and triple candlestick patterns and confirmation patterns, enabling traders to recognize signals for potential market reversals or continuations.</p>
	</li>
	<li dir="ltr">
	<p dir="ltr" style="text-align:justify">Bullish candlestick patterns signal that prices are likely to rise, whereas bearish candlestick patterns indicate that prices might drop.</p>
	</li>
</ul>
                            </div>
